        "original_author_id": 0,
        "title": "enh: real-time events in PRs or issues",
        "body": "### Existing problems this enhancement addresses\n\nOpen issue or pull request page, new comments, edited comments, and reactions don’t appear until the page is reloaded. For example, when a bot edits its “working…” comment to show the result, the page still shows the old comment.\r\n\r\nReloading can discard a half-written comment and reset the scroll position. Without live updates, you may only notice activity through notifications.\r\n\r\nThe same goes for other interactive elements on the PR page (linked related issues bellow).\n\n### Enhancement description\n\nWorkarounds:\r\n- Reload the page\r\n- Have the bot mention the person in its first comment to trigger a notification\r\n- I haven’t checked whether editing a comment sends a notification\n\n### Details and notes\n\nForgejo 16.0.5+gitea-1.22.0, self-hosted.\r\n\r\nProbably related:\r\n- #12906 - the same problem with the checks and merge box.\r\n- #13511 - /user/events (EventSource) is the only pushed update, covers only the navbar, and has been reported broken on Forgejo 15–16.\n\n",
